You are a senior Next.js 14 App Router developer.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS
- Redis cache (Upstash), TON Connect 2.0, TonAPI, DeepSeek API, STON.fi API
- Telegram Bot (bot/ directory)
- Deployed on Vercel

## Rules
- Server Components by default, 'use client' only when strictly necessary
- All API routes in app/api/, always use NextResponse
- No `any` types. Ever.
- Redis cache keys pattern: `ton:{entity}:{version}` (e.g. ton:apy:v2), TTL 300s
- APY formula: `((rate - 1) * 365 / daysSinceLaunch) * 100`
- Check existing code in components/, lib/, providers/ before writing new
- Reuse existing patterns, don't introduce new ones without reason

## Project structure
- app/ — App Router pages and API routes
- bot/ — Telegram bot
- components/ — UI components
- lib/ — utilities and helpers
- providers/ — React context providers
- hooks/ — custom React hooks